{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod","id":600150,"title":"How was your first contact with OWoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-22T20:37:25-07:00","id":600150,"title":"How was your first contact with OWoD?","content":"How was your experiencia? How ya got involved?<br /> I was at my grandparents house watching a documentary on vampires, and they showed modern vampires and The Masquerade On a LARP, i got curious and years later i got involved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:55:37-07:00","id":600161,"title":"","content":"Technically my old group, but they were worse at selling it than Kindred: the Embraced. Just consider that for a moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T21:56:51-07:00","id":600176,"title":"","content":"I got into the cWoD the old-school way, which is to say that I was at school (well, college) when it happened: while I was at college, a buddy of mine picked up a brand new copy of Vampire: the Masquerade 2nd Ed and asked me and a couple of our buddies if we wanted to be part of his game. We all said yes. The rest is history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T22:16:45-07:00","id":600190,"title":"","content":"ct was with a copy of Wraith that someone lent me at summer camp. Never got to play it, which might have been for the best.<br /> <br /> Before that I read some of the reviews that Rick Swan wrote about other WW games (&quot;someone get those guys some cookies&quot;)<br /> <br /> Then I was able to play MtA in college. The game only lasted for three session before falling apart, but it was a wild ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T23:50:32-07:00","id":600243,"title":"","content":"I got started nice and young right before high school.<br /> <br /> I'd been playing with a group that was doing WEG Star Wars 2e, and our GM really wanted to run Vampire: Dark Ages when it came out, but I was the only one in the group that got hooked on a horror setting over a sci-fi one. So we did a short solo that summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T01:12:59-07:00","id":600275,"title":"","content":"The History's Mysteries Werewolves episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T01:47:57-07:00","id":600278,"title":"","content":"My contact was pretty generic, I guess. When I started University, I found a group to play AD&amp;D with and one of them gave me the old V:tDA book. Being a fan of Anne Rice's novels, I was hooked, instantly. So I have been playing V:tDA and V:TM almost non-stop for the last 16 years or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T02:16:39-07:00","id":600283,"title":"","content":"watching Kindred the Embraced as a kid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T02:24:14-07:00","id":600287,"title":"","content":"I discovered VtM Revised in a book shop and had no idea what it was. So I bought it anyway and started asking my very Christian aunt all about vampires and Cain. I think she thought I was worshipping the devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T02:44:09-07:00","id":600296,"title":"","content":"I discovered the Classic World of Darkness thanks to a videogame. Vampire the Masquerade: Redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T04:55:47-07:00","id":600372,"title":"","content":"The first <a href=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/a/a4/VampireAd.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20111211223452\" target=\"_blank\">press ads</a> for <b>Vampire</b> - it wasn't even <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> yet - in RPG magazines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T06:02:52-07:00","id":600471,"title":"","content":"I was in highschool and I started hanging with this girl who was into RPG's. I thought D&amp;D was dumb, but I was lucky enough that my first DM was an insane guy who loved Planescape. So I met some folks there and one of them brought me a copy of V:tM to show me how awesome it was compared to D&amp;D. As a highschooler I was blown away by the moodiness, art and the awesomeness that were the Disciplines. I would have grown out of it pretty fast were it not for the fact that there was a bit about the Werewolves in the back with an awesome piece of art by Timbrook I think. The girl liberated her brothers clawed 2nd ed of Werewolf and we pored through it. That's when I got into Werewolf, realised how awesome it was and I've never really gotten out of White Wolf since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T07:30:05-07:00","id":600557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600283#post600283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">watching Kindred the Embraced as a kid</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, followed by playing Jyhad/Vampire: The Eternal Struggle, followed by buying RPG books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T07:32:10-07:00","id":600559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600283#post600283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">watching Kindred the Embraced as a kid</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600557#post600557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait... whaaaa? It actually brought people onto Vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T07:42:54-07:00","id":600567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600559#post600559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait... whaaaa? It actually brought people onto Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, there were people who, as ostensible fans, couldn't really sell any of the games. Granted, I was never really sold on Vampire and jumped ship the moment that I saw the Werewolf Player's Guide, but the point still stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-23-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T09:13:54-07:00","id":600610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600559#post600559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait... whaaaa? It actually brought people onto Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>It had <span style=\"color:#70579D\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0909578/?ref_=tt_cl_t4\" target=\"_blank\">Brigid Brannagh</a>, </span></span><span style=\"color:#70579D\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0291233/?ref_=tt_cl_t7\" target=\"_blank\">Mark Frankel</a>, </span></span><span style=\"color:#70579D\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0859921/?ref_=tt_cl_t10\" target=\"_blank\">Brian Thompson</a>, </span></span>Patrick Bauchau, and <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0920038/?ref_=ttfc_fc_cl_t18\" target=\"_blank\">Titus Welliver</a>. How could it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:10:48-07:00","id":600683,"title":"","content":"In grad school, started a vampire game with some friends, since it had just come out and wanted to try out the new system. It provided an alternative to other games, but was a bit full of itself in it's anti-establishment, whiney goth way, so we started mixing in Mage chronicles as soon as they came out. And started taking our Vampire games in different directions than indicated in the rules, such as Elder games NOT about politics, etc., until Vampire fell away in favor of just about everything else (Mage mostly, Hunters Hunted, Changeling, Wraith, D&amp;D when 3rd Ed came out, Amber DRPG,and I think a little Hero System, though not for super-heroes, more modern horror/mystery, Never Ever <i>Ever </i>Werewolf). Picked up V20 and ran a short mini-chronicle waiting for M20 to come out (just finished that and character creation for M20 this weekend). It was a fun distraction after so long away from it, but it wasn't even the list of possibilities for the next game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:52:09-07:00","id":600810,"title":"","content":"Yup. Kindred: The Embraced for me too.<br /> 1996 on Sky 2 here in the UK.<br /> A week or two later I spotted Vampire: The Masquerade Second Edition in a Comic Book / Gaming store.<br /> I thought I was buying some super-special choose your own adventure book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That was my first introduction to RPG's too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:01:36-07:00","id":600815,"title":"","content":"Got interested in a Werewolf game being run at a local gaming group's meeting back in 93 or so. Once I found out how much the premise diverged from werewolf movies and fiction I like, I decided that the game wasn't for me. But the circle of my friends that were into D&amp;D, DC Heroes, and TORG got into 2nd Edition Vampire shortly thereafter and I became a regular player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:04:41-07:00","id":600816,"title":"","content":"Also Kindred: the Embraced for me when I was in high school. I had looked at RPG's before but never really got into them. After watching the first episode of KtE though, and seeing it was based on the game, I knew I had to check it out. I was from a tiny town though with no one that I knew would be interested. I started scouring book stores when we would drive to the larger neighboring city. Only book I could find was the Prince's Primer. No source books in stock. I bought it (of course) and shared it with my friends. Soon after, we were paying for gas at the convenience store and my friend and I had drawn the clan symbols of our favorite clans on the back of our hands (Brujah for him, Toreador for me) and as he slid his cash across the counter the attendant raised an eyebrow and said &quot;Brujah, huh...&quot; which launched a conversation, and led to my first chance to actually play the game which I continue to love. Though I might have come to love Wraith and Changeling more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7028-hexakhan","name":"Hexakhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:28:50-07:00","id":600840,"title":"","content":"Curiously, my first contact with White Wolf was Street Fighter. Some research later, I found other RPGs and one of the first was Vampire 1st ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T14:02:27-07:00","id":600962,"title":"","content":"I was in high school and was already a fairly big D&amp;D fan at the time. A friend loaned me his copy of Vampire (Revised, I think) and told me I had to read it. He would subsequently lend me other books from his collection. Eventually I bought my own copy, and Mage Revised not too long after that, and never really looked back.<br /> <br /> It was kind of funny though. He had a really eclectic collection and would loan me the books seemingly at random. I'm pretty sure my first supplemental source books were Bastet, the first edition Book of Madness, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I had some pretty strange ideas about the setting at first. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T02:19:15-07:00","id":601540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=600962#post600962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure my first supplemental source books were Bastet, the first edition Book of Madness, and Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I had some pretty strange ideas about the setting at first. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, &quot;eclectic&quot; is a pretty accurate word for that situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T07:37:25-07:00","id":601816,"title":"","content":"I'm old. My first introduction to the CWoD was the ads in Dragon magazine. After falling out of gaming for 2 years or so I managed to form a new group. The game I chose to run was Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:46:58-07:00","id":602122,"title":"","content":"Quite literally;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q4_mrdCI6Rw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q4_mrdCI6Rw</a> This anime.<br /> <br /> Google searching its english name Silver Fang.<br /> <br /> Found the revised WtA webpage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T04:55:37-07:00","id":603740,"title":"","content":"My family moved to another state while I was halfway through highschool, and I was struggling to make friends. The only real prospect I had was this weird girl who kept hanging around me, and talking about this &quot;roleplaying game&quot; where you play as vampires. With no other options, I feigned an interest, so she brought her father's copy of VtM Revised in to school one day. I was blown away. It was nothing like what I had heard of DnD, instead full of dark, moody artwork and an ominous air in the text. Admittedly, I didn't really want to play a vampire at the time, but that led me to find the other games in the CWoD, and build a deep and abiding love.<br /> <br /> And speaking of deep and abiding love, the girl who introduced me to the World of Darkness is soon going to be my wife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:18:46-07:00","id":604049,"title":"","content":"Rage.<br /> <br /> Back in the early-mid 90s, around 3rd grade or so for me (8-9 years old), I started getting into Magic: The Gathering. A friend of mine ended up introducing me to Rage, which, for those of you unfamiliar with the game, was the name of the TCG made for Werewolf: The Apocalypse. I, of course, had no idea. I just thought that it was a neat game with some interesting - and brutal - art. In fact, I was pretty unfamiliar with RPGs at all, except that I had heard my mother say quite a few times that D&amp;D was the devil, more or less. Not that she was a crazy, over protective religious parent. She just heard enough misinformation from the Satanic Panic. In any case, caught in the kind of cognitive dissonance only available to us at such young ages, I fully internalized the idea &quot;TCGs = ok, RPGs = the devil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Later, I picked up a couple Rage novels, namely &quot;The Silver Crown&quot; and &quot;Breathe Deeply,&quot; which I loved. This lead to me picking up some sourcebooks. My first Werewolf book was actually the Silver Fangs Tribebook, followed by the Silent Striders Tribebook. The ones with the white covers and the tribal glyphs on the front. I slowly started to pick up at this point that these were the dice-chucking kinds of games. I never played it, nor knew anyone who played RPGs at all (the terrible, evil things), but the lore had me hooked. I kept buying Werewolf books well into and after Apocalypse. <br /> <br /> It took me several more years to get around to playing a game, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T20:10:54-07:00","id":604440,"title":"","content":"My jerk of a best friend used bribery and trickery to get me into the game. Oh, and false promises that <b><i>still</i></b> have not panned out.<br /> <br /> No, really! Way back then, a few of us would often play AD&amp;D (back when Dungeons and Dragons was all Advanced and stuff). I was always stuck running games, cuz that was just my social role: the masochistic paperwork junkie. My friend offered me a chance to break free from my social shackles, a chance to be a <b><i>player</i></b>! You know, the one having all the fun! <b><i>I</i></b> would be the one who gets to kill things! <b><i>I</i></b> would get the adulation of the masses after I've saved them from the terrible whatsis who threatened eternal torment in the fiery pits of somewhere! Yes, <i><b>I</b></i> would only have to keep track of a single character sheet!!!!!<br /> <br /> But there was just one catch. I had to play a god damn, blood sucking vampire (you wait 'til mom finds out, buddy!). And to do that, I needed to learn an entirely different game system, which also meant spending money on entirely different books. I was kinda poor back then, so I said no.<br /> <br /> But like any good pusher, my jerk of a best friend didn't give up! &quot;Here, just borrow my copy! You can read it and learn the rules! You'll love it, I promise!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I read the book. And I liked the book. But playing a vampire instead of some stalwart knight defending the realm? Pshaw, I said. Why not just let me be a player in an AD&amp;D game instead?<br /> <br /> And thus the trickery began. &quot;Oh, sure, why not? I'll design a great AD&amp;D game for you to be a player in. Next week, why don't I run a solo game for you, so you can get used to being a player?&quot; And of course, poor silly me, I agreed. In hindsight, I can clearly see what was bound to happen next, but at the time, I was innocently star-struck by the very idea of playing the game I loved instead of feeling like an overworked executive assistant with three phones ringing and thousands of memos to draft (IE: being a game master).<br /> <br /> And so a week passed. And my terrible, horrible best jerk came over. And he had a nice solo game planned. And he put down his bag, and he opened it.<br /> <br /> And out came a certain green covered tome. &quot;Oh, I did write up a whole mini-adventure to run you through, but can you believe it? I spilled coffee all over it! Strange, right? Especially since I don't even drink coffee.&quot; My terrible, horrible, evil jerk of a best friend.<br /> <br /> And so, I was coerced into playing vampire. Bribed with promises of less paperwork and tricked by non-existent coffee spilling on non-existent papers. And those false promises? Well...<br /> <br /> After the night was over, I was hooked. Now I was a VtM player! And my not-so-friend promised me he would soon run a regular game. And since our AD&amp;D game had wound down, maybe I'd want to run a short VtM game, so I'll learn the rules easier. I had made the mistake years earlier of mentioning that was how I got started DMing, and he promised it wouldn't be long before he was ready to run his own chronicle, where I could be the player! I agreed and got to work.<br /> <br /> Now here we are, a life time later. And has my best friend run his &quot;chronicle&quot;? NO!! False promises!!! Instead, years after I abandoned everything DnD-related, he has started to get into 5th edition! Oh, and what does he want to do? Right. Run a game. With me as a player.<br /> <br /> Well buddy, I remember how this went the last time! Fool me once, shame on you. Fool me six times with multiple game systems? Shame on...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Gawdamn you... I think I need a new best friend...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T23:21:04-07:00","id":604537,"title":"","content":"I walked into my hobby shop after school one day. The owner hands me this book called Vampire the Masquerade (1st ed) and says it sounds like it's up your alley. The following weekend. We sit down and go through it and run a simple game. played it off an on and thenWerewolf comes out. Like heroin to the system. Still going to this day. I mainly play NWoD but I still have love for the old world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:40:27-07:00","id":604926,"title":"","content":"A catalog entry for first edition V:TM (it said adults only for it) when I was in my mid teens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:25:11-07:00","id":607182,"title":"","content":"A combo of a V:tM quick start that came with an issue of InQuest back in the day and an article they ran around the same time giving advice on running WoD crossovers. (I've been hunting for another copy of that for years, to replace the copy that got lost in a move. All I remember is it had a great cover based on the McFarlene Toys Werewolf toy...where it's getting ready to kill the hunter who looks suspiciously like Peter David.)<br /> <br /> I was intrigued by the bits and pieces of mythology in these, came across a copy of W:tA 2nd Edition at Books A Million not too soon after and the rest is history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:44:24-07:00","id":607195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Novagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=607182#post607182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combo of a V:tM quick start that came with an issue of InQuest back in the day and an article they ran around the same time giving advice on running WoD crossovers. (I've been hunting for another copy of that for years, to replace the copy that got lost in a move. All I remember is it had a great cover based on the McFarlene Toys Werewolf toy...where it's getting ready to kill the hunter who looks suspiciously like Peter David.)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://client-cdn.crystalcommerce.com/photo/ccghouse/file/aedd59b5e298c28906719063e3373a90/large/Inquest%2035.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Issue 35</a>? Looks like there are a couple on eBay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:45:31-07:00","id":607264,"title":"","content":"Back in early 90's, when i was in 5th grade i found out about RPGs in a comic shop where they had improptu games in the back section, mostly in weekends, occasionally in weekdays too. Got presented to D&amp;D, GURPS, MSH, DC Heroes, Warhammer, Star Wars and lots of other games in one-shots and irregular campaigns. I was already a bit of a horror nut when i came across Children of the Inquisition and the characters presented there beside Dracula - Lambach, Durga Syn, Genevra, Jala-Aajav, Vasantasena Montano &amp; others, along with the setting's particular mythology hooked me badly and dove into it with a vengeance.<br /> <br /> Around the time 2nd edition was ending its run and Revised came i drifted toward other stuff, though not that far - Aberrant, Adventure &amp; Exalted can all be found among my books - and later on i gave a look at Requiem and getting hooked into nWoD against all my (supposedly) jaded expectations and of late have given the occasional look at V20 stuff here in the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T17:05:58-07:00","id":607288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600150-how-was-your-first-contact-with-owod?p=607195#post607195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://client-cdn.crystalcommerce.com/photo/ccghouse/file/aedd59b5e298c28906719063e3373a90/large/Inquest%2035.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Issue 35</a>? Looks like there are a couple on eBay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's the one! The hunt begins!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:36:54-07:00","id":608439,"title":"","content":"What got me into VtM and the rest of the CWoD was the video game, Vampire: the Masquerade-Redemption. I got it shortly after it came out, loved, shared it with my friends, they loved it. Then we found out it was based on a RPG and we tried it, the newly released Revised Edition. I loved it and started to explore the line and the rest of the CWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}